iceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":29},{"title":"Fetch Request - Scoped, Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.RequestAPI.md","line":30},{"title":"Fetch RequestInit - Scoped, Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.RequestInitAPI.md","line":31},{"title":"Fetch Response - Scoped,Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.ResponseAPI.md","line":32},{"title":"Available system properties","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/r_AvailableSystemProperties.md","line":34},{"title":"Server API reference","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/api-server.md","line":36},{"title":"Fetch Headers - append\\(String name, String value\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":42},{"title":"Fetch Headers - set\\(String name, String value\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":94},{"title":"Fetch Headers - values\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":429},{"title":"Fetch Headers - append\\(String name, String value\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":464},{"title":"Fetch Headers - keys\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.md","line":507}],"metadata":{"title":"Fetch Headers - Scoped, Global","description":"The Fetch Headers API allows you to retrieve, set, add to, and remove headers from a list of request or response headers.The Headers\\(\\) constructor creates a new, empty Headers object. You can also create and pre-populate a new Headers object with list of HTTP headers using the init parameter.Adds a new value to an existing header inside a Headers object, or adds the header if it does not already exist.Deletes a header from the current Headers object.Returns an iterator allowing you to cycle through all key-value pairs \\(represented with strings\\) contained in the Headers object.Executes a callback function once per each key/value pair in the Headers object.Returns a string of all header values of a specified Headers object, or returns null if the header does not exist.Returns all Set-Cookie headers associated with a response.Returns a Boolean indicating whether a Headers object contains the given header.Returns an iterator allowing you to cycle through all keys contained in a Headers object.Updates a value of an existing header inside the Headers object, or creates a new header with the given value if the header does not already exist.Returns an iterator allowing you to cycle through all header values contained in the Headers object.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/server-api-reference/Fetch.HeadersAPI.html","release":"australia","product":"Server API Reference","classification":"server-api-reference","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":9,"breadcrumb":["Server API reference","API reference","API implementation and reference"],"tags":["#api-reference","#glidesystem","#gliderecord","#server-side","#glide","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":